# Normalise line endings in the repo.
#
# CRLF cost three substitutions in Chunk 7.5 alone. The mechanism: a .sql file
# saved with CRLF on Windows is applied verbatim, so the function body stored in
# Postgres contains \r\n. A later migration that rewrites that body through
# pg_get_functiondef() and matches on a literal written with \n then matches
# NOTHING — and, being a substitution, fails open unless a guard catches it (G15).
#
# 102 function bodies in the live database already carry CRLF from before this
# rule. Those are not rewritten here: normalising them means replacing 102
# SECURITY DEFINER bodies, which is a deliberate sweep rather than a side effect
# of adding a config file. New ones will be LF.
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
